Package: CausalState
Type: Package
Title: Sequential Doubly Robust and Infinite-Dimensional TMLE Estimators for State-Aware Longitudinal Modified Treatment Policies
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Sebastiaan",
           family = "Blank",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "sebastiaan.bank@mail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9115-2138"))
Description: Implements Sequential Doubly Robust (SDR) and infinite-dimensional
    Targeted Maximum Likelihood (iTMLE) estimators for longitudinal modified treatment
    policies in settings with absorbing state transitions, such as ICU, ward,
    or emergency department care episodes. Treatment is permitted in active
    states and becomes structurally inapplicable after transition to an
    absorbing state (e.g. discharge or death). Supports asymmetric g- and
    Q-model regularisation, k-fold cross-fitting, and pluggable SuperLearner
    ensembles via included custom learner wrappers.
